Subject: [PATCH 06/10] fix(Performance Menu): hide TDP, thermal and power
 profile controls the GPU does not have

On a GPU the APU database does not know (any SoC GPU, e.g. Adreno on a
Snapdragon handheld) the TDP sliders, the thermal throttle slider and the
power profile dropdown were shown anyway, with ranges of -1 and writes to
properties PowerStation does not export for that card.

Show each only when HardwareManager says the GPU has it (tdp_capable,
tj_temp_capable, power_profile_capable). AMD and Intel APUs found in the
database are unchanged.

Such a GPU also has no power profiles, which the menu assumed it always
had: the apply timer indexed the empty profile list (aborting, so no
setting was ever applied or saved), and the default profile for the
mode toggle came back null and was dereferenced. Treat an empty list as
"no power profile" instead.
---
 core/ui/common/quick_bar/performance_menu.gd | 48 +++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

